WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.962
A setting someone clicked once has no
history, no review and no drift check.

2
00:00:04.962 --> 00:00:07.522
So the program deploys this one from code,

3
00:00:07.522 --> 00:00:11.963
and keeps its list of logged categories
in the repository as the record.

4
00:00:11.963 --> 00:00:13.025
Then retention.

5
00:00:13.025 --> 00:00:15.583
Here's a trap that catches
a lot of templates:

6
00:00:15.583 --> 00:00:19.988
the retention field on a diagnostic
setting no longer does anything at all.

7
00:00:19.988 --> 00:00:22.795
Retention is set per
table in the workspace,

8
00:00:22.795 --> 00:00:27.863
at least six months searchable and a year
retrievable, to meet the logging memo.

9
00:00:27.863 --> 00:00:31.988
Of course, a setting that saved
isn't proof anything is arriving.

10
00:00:31.988 --> 00:00:33.100
That's next.
